    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for June 14th is anchored by three high-upside plays that capitalize on favorable park factors and defensive vulnerabilities. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) earns the top spot on our board today, buoyed by a strong 4.93 xERA matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano and a significant boost from his dynamic platoon profile. **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) also stand out as elite options; **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a favorable wind-out scenario and the hitter-friendly conditions against Buehler, while **Jonathan Aranda**\u2019s projected #2 spot and robust 0.378 xwOBA make him a primary engine for our Roto categories. **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.21) remains a high-floor play, as the favorable 4.72 xERA of Abbott provides a perfect environment for him to exploit the base paths, a crucial factor given our emphasis on stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Drew Gilbert** (39.97), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.02). While **Drew Gilbert**\u2019s projections are solid, the combination of a pending lineup and a less favorable L/L platoon profile against Ryan Rolison relegated him to the bench. Conversely, **Gavin Sheets** (59.89) is a fringe-start candidate who stays in the lineup primarily due to the weather-aided boost; the combination of wind-out conditions and an exploitable matchup against Rogers elevates his ceiling just enough to stay in the rotation. Managers should remain vigilant regarding **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman**; both rely on assumed batting orders against Rolison, and any shift in the official lineup could quickly swing their daily efficiency scores below our marginal threshold. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Cal Raleigh** still sidelined, we are relying on our depth to maintain our standing in the scarce SB and HR categories.",
